Find the value of the following limit:
\[\lim_{x\to1}\frac{f(x)-f(1)}{x-1}.\]

\begin{align*}
\prod\limits_{k=1}^\infty (1 + x^{2^k}) &= \lim_{n \to \infty} \prod\limits_{k=1}^n (1 + x^{2^k}) \\
&= \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{1 - x^{2^{n+1}}}{1 - x^2} \\
&= \frac{1}{1 - x^2} = \frac{1{1 - x^2}}
\end{align*}
Final answer: \frac{1}{1 - x^2}

